# Unixsee monorepo

Flat deployables at repo root: `admin-panel/`, `client/`, `backend/`, `agent/`, `monitoring-agent/`, `docs/`.

## Ownership

- `admin-panel/` — staff Next.js UI
- `client/` — customer / public Next.js UI
- `backend/` — NestJS control plane
- `agent/` — Phase 1 VPS agent (PRD; build from scratch)
- `monitoring-agent/` — monitoring edge agent (existing; develop later)
- `docs/` — canonical documentation

Do not invent `apps/` or `packages/` without an ADR.

## Trust boundaries

- NestJS owns auth, persistence, orchestration, and agent validation.
- Admin and client never talk to agents or VPS hosts.
- Read `docs/architecture/overview.md` and `docs/architecture/monorepo.md`.

## Phase

- `backend/` is an active NestJS control plane; follow
  `docs/backend/modules-and-routes.md` and ADRs 0004–0005.
- Next.js Nest integration:
  `docs/architecture/decisions/0011-client-nest-auth-integration.md` (`client/`),
  `docs/architecture/decisions/0012-admin-nest-auth-integration.md`
  (`admin-panel/`). Shared hybrid transport: ADR 0010.

## Docs over invention

- Start from `docs/README.md` and `AGENTS.md`.
- Put lasting detail in `docs/`; keep rules thin.
- Do not invent APIs that conflict with `docs/backend/modules-and-routes.md`,
  or unavailable root scripts.
